From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:46:31 -0500
Subject: feat: a pin's redirected link peeks, and a screenshot takes the peek

A link from a pin that the server sends to another site stayed in the pin,
because the throttle judged only the link. It now judges each redirect by the
same rules and opens the peek at the destination, so the address that
redirected is not asked twice. A sign-in stays in the pin, including whatever
the steps after a sign-in page lead to.

The screenshot keys captured the pin under a peek over the page. They take
the peek on top.

Why: S-93 (peek P22, P23; PLAN.md CMD-29, WIN-18).

Removable when: peeks go.
